- Use setuptools for Python package development and distribution with proper configuration.
- Define comprehensive package metadata including name, version, description, and author information.
- Implement proper dependency management with install_requires and extras_require specifications.
- Use entry points for command-line scripts and plugin discovery mechanisms.
- Configure proper package discovery with find_packages() or explicit package listings.
- Implement version management strategies with dynamic versioning or static version strings.
- Use proper classifiers for package categorization and Python version compatibility.
- Configure build requirements and build-time dependencies with build-system table.
- Implement proper package data inclusion with package_data and MANIFEST.in files.
- Use setuptools extensions for complex build processes and custom build steps.

